Verse 1:
[Eb]There'll be no dark valley when [Ab]Jesus [Eb]comes,
[Eb]There'll be no dark valley when [Bb]Jesus comes,
There'll be [Eb]no dark valley when [Ab]Jesus [Eb]comes,
[Bb]To [Eb]gather [Cm]His [Bb]loved ones [Eb]home.
[Eb]To gather His [Ab]loved [Eb]ones home, ([Bb7]safe [Eb]home)
[Eb]To gather His [F7]loved ones [Bb]home, ([Bb7]safe [Eb]home).
[Bb7]There'll [Eb]be no dark valley when [Ab]Jesus [Eb]comes,
[Bb]To [Eb]gather [Cm]His [Bb]loved ones [Eb]home.

Refrain:
[Eb]To gather [Ab]His loved [Eb]ones home,
[Eb]To gather His [Bb]loved ones home.
[Eb]There'll be [Ab]no dark valleys [Eb]when Jesus comes,
[Bb]To [Eb]gather [Cm]His [Bb]loved [Eb]ones home.

Verse 2:
[Eb]There'll be [Ab]no more sorrow [Eb]when Jesus comes,
[Eb]There'll be no more [Bb]sorrow when Jesus comes,
[Eb]There'll be [Ab]a happy tomorrow [Eb]when Jesus comes,
[Bb]To [Eb]gather [Cm]His [Bb]loved [Eb]ones home.

Verse 3:
[Eb]There'll be [Ab]songs of greeting [Eb]when Jesus comes,
[Eb]There'll be songs of [Bb]greeting when Jesus comes,
[Eb]There'll be [Ab]songs of greeting [Eb]when Jesus comes,
[Bb]To [Eb]gather [Cm]His [Bb]loved [Eb]ones home.
